<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64385" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῦ</span></b> , τό, 
			Ion.
		
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Democr.
					19
				</span></i>
			: indecl., thirteenth (later twelfth) letter of
			the Gr. alphabet: as numeral <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ́</span>
			=
			<i><span class="en">
				40
			</span></i>, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">
				m'
			</span>
			=
			<i><span class="en">
				40
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				000
			</span></i>.—In Inscrr. M stands for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύριοι</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυριάς</span>:
			hence &lt;*&gt; for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεντακισμύριοι</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέντε
			μυριάδες</span>, <i><span class="en">
				50
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				000
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
